                    <div class="row">
                            <div class="col-lg-12 col-sm-12">
                                  <div class="bg-transparent mb-5">
    <div class="pt-4">
      <h3 class="border-bottom border-2 border-light fw-bold pb-2 mb-3 position-relative title-with-icon">
        <i class="ico-zap me-3 fs-5"></i>Pacific Command Visits 1st SFG(A)
      </h3>
    </div>
    <div class="row">
      <div class="col-lg-6 col-md-6 col-sm-12 pt-4">
          <p class="card-text"><small class="link-secondary fst-italic text-break">https://www.dvidshub.net/image/9901478/pacific-command-visits-1st-sfga</small></p>
        <p class="card-text mh-150px overflow-auto stylized-scroll">
          <strong class="fw-bold">
            August 26, 2026
            &mdash;
          </strong>
          A U.S. Soldier assigned to 5th Security Force Assistance Brigade, explains the use of the Android Tactical Assault Kit (ATAK) in recent exercises to the Senior Enlisted Advisor of Pacific Command, United States Marine Corps Sgt. Major Eric Cook, right, at Joint Base Lewis-McChord, Washington, Aug. 28, 2026. This visit highlights the cooperation between 1st Special Forces Group (Airborne) and 5th SFAB who share a role in strengthening U.S. Army presence in the Pacific theater. 1st SFG(A) maintains highly lethal, rapidly deployable forces to execute the full spectrum of special operations alongside allies, partners, and the joint force as the preferred partner and premier special operations entity in the U.S. Pacific Command area of responsibility. (U.S. Army photo by Cpl Micah Wilson).
        </p>
          <a href="https://www.dvidshub.net/image/9901478/pacific-command-visits-1st-sfga"
            class="btn btn-primary"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >More Info <i class="ico-external-link fs-6 ms-2 mt-n1"></i></a>
      </div>
      <div class="col-lg-6 col-md-6 col-sm-12 pt-4">
          <img src="https://tak-gov-webapp-assets.s3.us-gov-west-1.amazonaws.com/crjwmoyhbalakqa33g36kl50y30k?response-content-disposition=inline%3B%20filename%3D%22pacific_cmd_visits_1st_sfg.jpg%22%3B%20filename%2A%3DUTF-8%27%27pacific_cmd_visits_1st_sfg.jpg&amp;response-content-type=image%2Fjpeg&amp;X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&amp;X-Amz-Credential=AKIATJSIUVX5SCHDUUNN%2F20260930%2Fus-gov-west-1%2Fs3%2Faws4_request&amp;X-Amz-Date=20260930T172521Z&amp;X-Amz-Expires=300&amp;X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&amp;X-Amz-Signature=f9f24ad3c70b98b989e1d88d94301c50848dd40d88260ba03e87b9f842ad2f18" class="text-end">
      </div>
    </div>
	</div> 
  <div class="bg-transparent mb-5">
    <div class="pt-4">
      <h3 class="border-bottom border-2 border-light fw-bold pb-2 mb-3 position-relative title-with-icon">
        <i class="ico-zap me-3 fs-5"></i>JRTC 26-10 JFE
      </h3>
    </div>
    <div class="row">
      <div class="col-lg-6 col-md-6 col-sm-12 pt-4">
          <p class="card-text"><small class="link-secondary fst-italic text-break">https://www.dvidshub.net/image/9935865/jrtc-26-10-jfe</small></p>
        <p class="card-text mh-150px overflow-auto stylized-scroll">
          <strong class="fw-bold">
            August 26, 2026
            &mdash;
          </strong>
          A Paratrooper assigned to 2nd Mobile Brigade Combat Team, 82nd Airborne Division assesses coordinates with an Android Tactical Assault Kit (ATAK) during a Joint Readiness Training Center (JRTC) rotation at Fort Polk, Louisiana. Paratroopers are tasked with attacking and defending themselves from enemy forces throughout the duration of JRTC in order to complete the mission at hand. (U.S. Army photo by Spc. Sebastian Johnston)
        </p>
          <a href="https://www.dvidshub.net/image/9935865/jrtc-26-10-jfe"
            class="btn btn-primary"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >More Info <i class="ico-external-link fs-6 ms-2 mt-n1"></i></a>
      </div>
      <div class="col-lg-6 col-md-6 col-sm-12 pt-4">
