                        <a href="https://www.dvidshub.net/image/9901478/pacific-command-visits-1st-sfga"
                            class="card-body link-light"
                            title="Pacific Command Visits 1st SFG(A)"
                            target="_blank"
                            rel="noopener noreferrer">
                            <h5 class="card-title fw-bold">Pacific Command Visits 1st SFG(A)&nbsp;→</h5>
                            <p class="news-url link-secondary fst-italic"><small>https://www.dvidshub.net/image/9901478/pacific-command-visits-1st-sfga</small></p>
                            <p class="card-text"><strong>August 26, 2026 &mdash;</strong> A U.S. Soldier assigned to 5th Security Force Assistance Brigade, explains the use of the Android Tactical Assault Kit (ATAK) in recent exercises to the Senior Enlisted Advisor of Pacific Command, United States Marine Corps Sgt. Major Eric Cook, right, at Joint Base Lewis-McChord, Washington, Aug. 28, 2026. This visit highlights the cooperation between 1st Special Forces Group (Airborne) and 5th SFAB who share a role in strengthening U.S. Army presence in the Pacific theater. 1st SFG(A) maintains highly lethal, rapidly deployable forces to execute the full spectrum of special operations alongside allies, partners, and the joint force as the preferred partner and premier special operations entity in the U.S. Pacific Command area of responsibility. (U.S. Army photo by Cpl Micah Wilson).</p>
                        </a>
